          "filename": "Inspecting a Sacramento River levee (8598950048).jpg",
          "caption": "Levee inspector Ryan Larson, with the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers Sacramento District, documents his findings during a routine levee inspection on the Sacramento River near Rio Vista, Calif., March 27, 2013. The results of U.S. Army Corps of Engineers levee inspections determine continued eligibility for federal aid in repairing levees damaged by floods or storms, and help communities understand and make informed decisions about their flood risk. Corps inspectors document all maintenance issues with GPS coordinates and photographs to help agencies that maintain levees prioritize and fix issues as quickly as possible. (U.S. Army photo by Chris Gray-Garcia/Released)",
